<mjml lang="en">
  <mj-head>
    <!--
      PROBE — CTA Hero (w/ heading): the heading-to-button gap in Outlook
      desktop (2026-09-28). Follows 856a2ec, which replaced a 4/8 `&nbsp;`
      spacer <p> under the h3 with 32px of bottom padding on the h3's own
      text cell. Chrome measured the gap 34px before and 32px after. Outlook
      desktop was never measured, before or after.

      Not a catalog page. Build, paste dist/probe_cta-heading-gap-outlook-2026-09-28_live.html
      into an EN email, send to EoA. Read the DELIVERED HTML first
      (display/email_html/<TEST_ID>), then the Word-engine renders
      (Outlook 2016 and 2019 at 120 DPI, Outlook 2021 Win11, M365 Win11,
      Office 365 Win10), then Apple Mail / iOS / Gmail web as controls.
      Light mode only; dark is out of scope.

      The head carries src/main.mjml's mj-attributes and its head-resident
      sheet verbatim (the `.wysiwyg div h3:last-child { margin-bottom: 0 }`
      rule is half of what is under test), plus styles.css.

      ══ CLAIMS
        C1  In every Word-engine Outlook the SHIPPED shape renders the gap at
            32px, as every other client does.
        C2  EN inlines `margin-bottom:0` onto the shipped h3 at send (the
            :last-child rule) and keeps `padding:0 0 32px` on its text cell.
        C3  (baseline, recorded, not pass/fail) what the OLD shape rendered in
            each Outlook, so the ledger knows how far the fix moved it there.

      ══ R — THE REAL BLOCK, on the kayak photo. Eyeball test.
        R1 SHIPPED  the block exactly as main.mjml ships it (856a2ec).
        R2 OLD      the pre-856a2ec markup: padding 0, spacer <p> under the h3.
        PASS: in each Outlook, R1's gap looks like Apple Mail's R1.

      ══ M — METERED TWINS. Same group geometry, flat Grass ground, and
         palette paint so the gap is a band you can count:
           MOSS   #CEE4C5  the h3's own box (its padding included)
           SKY    #5DD8D8  the text cell; Sky BELOW the Moss box is the gap
           SUN    #F7931E  the 32px ruler at the top of the series
         Gap in px = (Sky band pixels / Sun ruler pixels) x 32, which holds at
         any DPI because both scale together.
        M1 SHIPPED  as R1.                                   Expect 32 everywhere.
        M2 OLD      as R2.                                   Chrome: 34. Outlook: C3.
        M3 CONTROL  as M1 with margin:0 authored on the h3.  Expect 32 everywhere.
        Reading: M1 = M3 = 32 → C1 PASSES. M3 = 32 but M1 ≠ 32 → the inlined
        margin did not reach the h3 in that client (check C2 in the delivered
        HTML). M3 ≠ 32 → Word is not honouring the cell padding itself.

      VERDICT (2026-09-28, sent through EN, EoA r9Xx6T…, 19 clients). Delivered
      HTML read first; M bands pixel-counted down the centre of the Sky cell.
        C2 PASSES. EN inlined `margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0` onto the R1
          and M1 h3s and kept `padding: 0 0 32px` on their cells. R2/M2 got
          `margin-top: 0` only: the spacer <p> was their last child. EN's
          inliner fingerprint (mso-table-lspace on td) sits on 48 cells, so
          the send went through EN.
        C1 PASSES. M1 = M3 = 32px in Outlook 2016 and 2019 at 120 DPI (40
          device px against a 40-row ruler, 1.25x) and in Outlook 2021 and
          M365 Win11 (32 against 32), the same as Apple Mail 16, M365 Mac,
          iOS 26, Gmail web and Outlook.com. R1 matches by eye. Office 365
          Win10 was not in this send.
        C3 recorded. The OLD shape rendered 25.6-27px in every Word engine
          (2016 26.4, 2019 25.6, 2021 27, M365 27) against 34px everywhere
          else. Word gave the h3 its own bottom spacing, about 19px (27 minus
          the 8px spacer; inferred, and consistent with Word's 14pt auto
          spacing), where browsers apply 1em = 26px. The fix moved Word up
          5-6px and every other client down 2px: the cross-client spread went
          from 7-8px to 0.
      Archived the same day.
    -->
    <mj-raw>
      <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark" />
      <meta name="supported-color-schemes" content="light dark" />
      <meta name="format-detection" content="telephone=no" />
    </mj-raw>
    <mj-attributes>
      <mj-text
        color="#000000"
        font-size="18px"
        font-weight="400"
        font-family="Tahoma, sans-serif"
        line-height="24px"
        css-class="wysiwyg"
      />
      <mj-button width="auto"
        css-class="button"
        font-size="18px"
        font-weight="700"
        font-family="Tahoma, sans-serif"
        line-height="22px"
        border-radius="100px"
        inner-padding="12px 16px"
        letter-spacing="1px"
        color="#ffffff"
        background-color="#006837"
      />
      <mj-image
        padding="0" />

      <!-- Reusable variants — apply with mj-class="*" -->
      <mj-class
        name="caption"
        font-size="10px"
        line-height="16px"
        padding="4px 0 0 0"
      />
    </mj-attributes>
    <mj-raw>
      <style type="text/css" data-en-tools-template-css>
        /* HEAD-RESIDENT rules (catalogued 2026-08-24, user decision same day;
           see future-enhancements "Head-vs-block CSS"). Everything here must
           pass two tests: absence REVEALS or DUPLICATES content or breaks a
           mechanism every email relies on, and it would never be fixed by
           swapping the Template Styles block. Fix-by-block-swap rules stay in
           styles.css. EN inlines top-level rules from this head exactly as it
           does the CSS Editor field (measured 2026-08-24, EoA XXhlSbq1e…). */

        /* RTE margin containment — the bottom-only pacing model rests on
           these; without them every RTE block grows phantom margins. */
        /* Block elements only, enumerated (2026-09-25, EoA d0S0nH…): the old
           `*:first-child` / `*:last-child` also matched INLINE runs, so EN
           inlined margin-top/bottom:0 onto <strong>, <u>, <a>, <br>, and Word
           lets an inline run's margin zero its whole paragraph's spacing —
           adjacent formatted paragraphs ran together in Outlook (BugHerd 296).
           Enumerated rather than `div > *` because §2d bans child combinators. */
        .wysiwyg div p:first-child,
        .wysiwyg div h1:first-child,
        .wysiwyg div h2:first-child,
        .wysiwyg div h3:first-child,
        .wysiwyg div h4:first-child,
        .wysiwyg div h5:first-child,
        .wysiwyg div h6:first-child,
        .wysiwyg div ul:first-child,
        .wysiwyg div ol:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
        .wysiwyg div p:last-child,
        .wysiwyg div h1:last-child,
        .wysiwyg div h2:last-child,
        .wysiwyg div h3:last-child,
        .wysiwyg div h4:last-child,
        .wysiwyg div h5:last-child,
        .wysiwyg div h6:last-child,
        .wysiwyg div ul:last-child,
        .wysiwyg div ol:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

        /* Copy over a photo must be white even in an email built without the
           styles block (user decision 2026-08-24: relocated rather than
           re-authored inline). */
        .overlay h1, .overlay h2, .overlay h3, .overlay h4, .overlay h5,
        .overlay h6, .overlay span, .overlay p, .overlay a { color: #fff; }

        /* Viewport fork: hide twice, reveal once, in this order. */
        .mobile-only { display: none; }

        /* Mode fork (light/dark twins): the plain hide half. The dark twins
           sit in downlevel-revealed conditionals, so without this every
           non-Outlook client renders BOTH twins. Repaints stay in styles.css
           — only the swap mechanism lives here. */
        .dark-only { display: none; }
        :root { color-scheme: light dark; supported-color-schemes: light dark; }

        @media (max-width: 9998px) {
          .mobile-only { display: none !important; }
        }
        @media only screen and (max-width: 599px) {
          .desktop-only { display: none !important; }
          .mobile-only { display: block !important; }
        }
        /* Mode-fork reveals. These two blocks are the FIRST occurrence of
           their conditions, so styles.css's same-condition repaint blocks
           fold up to these positions at send — swap first, repaints after,
           which is byte-for-byte today's order inside styles.css. */
        @media only screen and (max-width: 9999px) {
          [data-ogsc] .dark-only { display: block !important; }
          [data-ogsc] .light-only { display: none !important; }
        }
        @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
          .light-only { display: none !important; }
          .dark-only { display: block !important; }
        }
      </style>
    </mj-raw>
    <mj-include path="../styles.css" type="css" />
  </mj-head>

  <mj-body background-color="#F5FAF1">
    <mj-raw><div style="color:#000000;background-color:#F5FAF1;margin:0;padding:0;"><div class="email-ground" style="background-color:#F5FAF1;margin:0;padding:0;"></mj-raw>

    <mj-section padding="16px 32px 8px"><mj-column><mj-text padding="0"><p style="font-size:14px;line-height:18px;color:#362229;margin:0;"><b>PROBE — CTA Hero (w/ heading) gap.</b> R = the real block. M = metered twins: gap = Sky band under the Moss heading box, measured against the Sun 32px ruler.</p></mj-text></mj-column></mj-section>

    <!-- ══ R1 SHIPPED ══ -->
    <mj-section padding="16px 32px 8px"><mj-column><mj-text padding="0"><p style="font-size:14px;line-height:18px;color:#362229;margin:0;"><b>R1 SHIPPED</b>: the block as main.mjml ships it (32px cell padding)</p></mj-text></mj-column></mj-section>
    <mj-wrapper background-color="#362229" padding="0">
      <mj-section css-class="image-block block" background-url="assets/photo-kayak.jpg" background-size="cover" background-repeat="no-repeat" background-position="center center" padding="32px 0 32px">
        <mj-group data-no-direction-toggle>
          <mj-column width="32px">&nbsp;</mj-column>
          <mj-column vertical-align="top" width="240px">
            <mj-image data-display-toggle css-class="light-only" src="assets/logo-tpl_color-light-green-text.png" alt="Trust for Public Land" href="https://tpl.org" width="144px" padding="0 8px 8px 0" align="left" />
            <mj-raw><!--[if !mso]><!--></mj-raw>
            <mj-image css-class="dark-only" src="assets/logo-tpl_color-light-green-text.png" alt="Trust for Public Land" href="https://tpl.org" width="144px" padding="0 8px 8px 0" align="left" data-style-dark-mode />
            <mj-raw><!--<![endif]--></mj-raw>
          </mj-column>
          <mj-column vertical-align="top" width="296px">
            <mj-text align="center" css-class="wysiwyg advocacy-box" padding="0 0 32px">
              <h3 style="color:#ffffff;padding:12px 8px 0;">Lorem Ipsum Dolor Sit Amet</h3>
            </mj-text>
            <mj-button width="auto" href="https://tpl.org" align="center" padding="0" color="#ffffff" background-color="#006837">LEARN MORE</mj-button>
          </mj-column>
          <mj-column width="32px">&nbsp;</mj-column>
        </mj-group>
      </mj-section>
    </mj-wrapper>

    <!-- ══ R2 OLD ══ -->
    <mj-section padding="24px 32px 8px"><mj-column><mj-text padding="0"><p style="font-size:14px;line-height:18px;color:#362229;margin:0;"><b>R2 OLD</b>: the pre-fix markup (4/8 spacer paragraph, no padding)</p></mj-text></mj-column></mj-section>
    <mj-wrapper background-color="#362229" padding="0">
      <mj-section css-class="image-block block" background-url="assets/photo-kayak.jpg" background-size="cover" background-repeat="no-repeat" background-position="center center" padding="32px 0 32px">
        <mj-group data-no-direction-toggle>
          <mj-column width="32px">&nbsp;</mj-column>
          <mj-column vertical-align="top" width="240px">
            <mj-image data-display-toggle css-class="light-only" src="assets/logo-tpl_color-light-green-text.png" alt="Trust for Public Land" href="https://tpl.org" width="144px" padding="0 8px 8px 0" align="left" />
            <mj-raw><!--[if !mso]><!--></mj-raw>
            <mj-image css-class="dark-only" src="assets/logo-tpl_color-light-green-text.png" alt="Trust for Public Land" href="https://tpl.org" width="144px" padding="0 8px 8px 0" align="left" data-style-dark-mode />
            <mj-raw><!--<![endif]--></mj-raw>
          </mj-column>
          <mj-column vertical-align="top" width="296px">
            <mj-text align="center" css-class="wysiwyg advocacy-box" padding="0">
              <h3 style="color:#ffffff;padding:12px 8px 0;">Lorem Ipsum Dolor Sit Amet</h3>
              <p style="margin:0;font-size:4px;line-height:8px;">&nbsp;</p>
            </mj-text>
            <mj-button width="auto" href="https://tpl.org" align="center" padding="0" color="#ffffff" background-color="#006837">LEARN MORE</mj-button>
          </mj-column>
          <mj-column width="32px">&nbsp;</mj-column>
        </mj-group>
      </mj-section>
    </mj-wrapper>

    <!-- ══ RULER ══ -->
    <mj-section padding="32px 32px 8px"><mj-column><mj-text padding="0"><p style="font-size:14px;line-height:18px;color:#362229;margin:0;"><b>RULER</b>: the Sun bar below is 32px</p></mj-text></mj-column></mj-section>
    <mj-section background-color="#F7931E" padding="0"><mj-column><mj-spacer height="32px" /></mj-column></mj-section>

    <!-- ══ M1 SHIPPED ══ -->
    <mj-section padding="24px 32px 8px"><mj-column><mj-text padding="0"><p style="font-size:14px;line-height:18px;color:#362229;margin:0;"><b>M1 SHIPPED</b>: expect a 32px Sky band</p></mj-text></mj-column></mj-section>
    <mj-section background-color="#8CC63F" padding="32px 0 32px">
        <mj-group>
          <mj-column width="32px">&nbsp;</mj-column>
          <mj-column vertical-align="top" width="240px">&nbsp;</mj-column>
          <mj-column vertical-align="top" width="296px">
            <mj-text align="center" css-class="wysiwyg advocacy-box" container-background-color="#5DD8D8" padding="0 0 32px">
              <h3 style="color:#362229;background-color:#CEE4C5;padding:12px 8px 0;">Lorem Ipsum Dolor Sit Amet</h3>
            </mj-text>
            <mj-button width="auto" href="https://tpl.org" align="center" padding="0" color="#ffffff" background-color="#006837">LEARN MORE</mj-button>
          </mj-column>
          <mj-column width="32px">&nbsp;</mj-column>
        </mj-group>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- ══ M2 OLD ══ -->
    <mj-section padding="24px 32px 8px"><mj-column><mj-text padding="0"><p style="font-size:14px;line-height:18px;color:#362229;margin:0;"><b>M2 OLD</b>: Chrome renders 34px; Outlook is what this measures</p></mj-text></mj-column></mj-section>
    <mj-section background-color="#8CC63F" padding="32px 0 32px">
        <mj-group>
          <mj-column width="32px">&nbsp;</mj-column>
          <mj-column vertical-align="top" width="240px">&nbsp;</mj-column>
          <mj-column vertical-align="top" width="296px">
            <mj-text align="center" css-class="wysiwyg advocacy-box" container-background-color="#5DD8D8" padding="0">
              <h3 style="color:#362229;background-color:#CEE4C5;padding:12px 8px 0;">Lorem Ipsum Dolor Sit Amet</h3>
              <p style="margin:0;font-size:4px;line-height:8px;">&nbsp;</p>
            </mj-text>
            <mj-button width="auto" href="https://tpl.org" align="center" padding="0" color="#ffffff" background-color="#006837">LEARN MORE</mj-button>
          </mj-column>
          <mj-column width="32px">&nbsp;</mj-column>
        </mj-group>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- ══ M3 CONTROL ══ -->
    <mj-section padding="24px 32px 8px"><mj-column><mj-text padding="0"><p style="font-size:14px;line-height:18px;color:#362229;margin:0;"><b>M3 CONTROL</b>: as M1, margin:0 authored on the heading; expect 32px</p></mj-text></mj-column></mj-section>
    <mj-section background-color="#8CC63F" padding="32px 0 32px">
        <mj-group>
          <mj-column width="32px">&nbsp;</mj-column>
          <mj-column vertical-align="top" width="240px">&nbsp;</mj-column>
          <mj-column vertical-align="top" width="296px">
            <mj-text align="center" css-class="wysiwyg advocacy-box" container-background-color="#5DD8D8" padding="0 0 32px">
              <h3 style="color:#362229;background-color:#CEE4C5;padding:12px 8px 0;margin:0;">Lorem Ipsum Dolor Sit Amet</h3>
            </mj-text>
            <mj-button width="auto" href="https://tpl.org" align="center" padding="0" color="#ffffff" background-color="#006837">LEARN MORE</mj-button>
          </mj-column>
          <mj-column width="32px">&nbsp;</mj-column>
        </mj-group>
    </mj-section>

    <mj-section padding="24px 32px 32px"><mj-column><mj-text padding="0"><p style="font-size:14px;line-height:18px;color:#362229;margin:0;">End of probe. Sky band = the gap. Sun bar = 32px.</p></mj-text></mj-column></mj-section>

    <mj-raw></div></div></mj-raw>
  </mj-body>
</mjml>
